  <h2>Deep Notes</h2>
  <p>Unpredictability</p>
  <p>Taken from <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Simulator_User_Group/Transcripts/2012.10.05" target="_blank">Simulator User Group/Transcripts/2012.10.05</a></p>
  <p>[16:24] <b>Andrew Linden</b>: the llApplyImpulse() is even more unpredictable</p>
  <p>[16:24] <b>Andrew Linden</b>: because it uses the legacy script "energy budget"</p>
  <p>[16:25] <b>Andrew Linden</b>: which will attenuate the results if the scripted object doesn't have enough "energy" to execute the impulse that it wants</p>
  <p>[16:25] <b>Andrew Linden</b>: also, that llApplyImpulse() has great griefing potential</p>
  <p>[16:25] <b>Andrew Linden</b>: so we hobbled it a long time ago with a very high energy consumption rate</p>
